    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23eb9264_87f9ca01",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 99,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-03-24T19:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wow, there\u0027s a lot of negatives in that sentence.  And it\u0027s also technically not true.  *ACPI* can\u0027t access that region, but there is a EC_CMD_READ_MEMMAP which works just fine from kernel and userland (on platforms with i2c or spi host buses, and even on mec1322).\n\nSuggest instead:\n\n/* ACPI is unable to access memory mapped data at or above\n * this offset due to limitations of the ACPI protocol.  Do\n * not place data in the range 0xe0 - 0xfe which might be\n * needed by ACPI. */\n#define EC_MEMMAP_NO_ACPI 0xe0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "9bfb4f63214ab58c8a416ef266e3d512cce7fd71",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
